      "content": "AI will use more power than Japan by 2027 ⚡\n\nBy 2027, AI data centers will consume more electricity than Japan — currently the world's fourth-largest power user.\n\nTraining GPT-4 alone used as much energy as 1,000 US homes consume in an entire year. Every AI query uses 10 times the electricity of a standard Google search.\n\nThe AI industry is projected to account for 4 to 8% of global electricity consumption by 2030.\n\nMicrosoft, Google, and Amazon are now investing in nuclear power plants — specifically to power their AI data centers. The existing power grid can't keep up.\n\nThe intelligence explosion has an electricity bill.\n\n#aifacts #ai #energy #nuclearpower #climatetech #artificialintelligence #datacenter #techtrends",
