      "_id": "69cd609a3e56aceadda04550",
      "latePostId": "69cce8361a483174d7e21fab",
      "content": "ChatGPT doesn't understand language 🤖 It predicts it.\n\nLarge language models work by predicting which token — a word or word fragment — statistically follows every previous token. One at a time. Repeated billions of times across over a trillion words of human text.\n\nThe model learns which patterns of words tend to precede which other patterns. That's it.\n\nWhat looks like reasoning, creativity, or understanding is an emergent property of prediction at massive scale.\n\nThere is no world model inside. No intent. No semantic comprehension. Just the most sophisticated autocomplete system ever built — running fast enough to appear intelligent.\n\nWhen AI surprises you, it's because the patterns at trillion-word scale generate outputs humans weren't expecting. Not because it understood the question.\n\n#aifacts #llm #chatgpt #artificialintelligence #howaiworks #machinelearning #aiexplained #tech",
