      "latePostId": "69cb89796be338f1f253e92d",
      "content": "A lawyer cited 6 AI-hallucinated cases in federal court 🤖\n\nA lawyer cited 6 AI-hallucinated cases in federal court 🤖\n\nIn 2023, a New York lawyer submitted legal briefs to a US federal court. Six of the cases cited were completely fabricated.\n\nChatGPT had invented them — case names, judges, rulings, citations — all generated with total confidence. When the judge asked for copies, the lawyer searched every major legal database. The cases didn't exist.\n\nThe lawyer admitted the source: ChatGPT.\n\nBoth lawyers were sanctioned $5,000 each. A federal judge wrote a 21-page opinion on AI hallucinations — the first time AI's confident wrongness had an official legal paper trail.\n\nAI doesn't know what it doesn't know. And it never sounds uncertain.\n\n#aifacts #chatgpt #ai #hallucination #legaltech #artificialintelligence #ailaw #techlegal",
